The Machine God is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] living in a fane deep in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. It is an old Heart, made long before the ones the Orgs make now, which are said to be weaker and to lack the powers that older Hearts hold.

Its body is the broken upper half of a mechanical man, torn off below the torso, with a glowing orb set in its chest. It speaks in a low, grinding voice, like metal dragged across metal, and it counts the followers of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] still in the strider as its enemies and would have them killed.

It was the eyes and ears of the strider's first inhabitants, watching and working within it. A spider, Vrax'leth, took up in its works and left it weak; that spider is dead. It says the strider was adrift far along the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Horizon]], a trap that was never sprung, and that a false god, [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], wormed its way into those people over years and centuries and took and changed them. What is left of them still crawls about the strider.

It sees what goes on within the strider but nothing above it. In return for the Party's help it has struck an accord with them and can speak to them directly, needing no totem, and it gave them a share of the same: a group telepathy that lets them speak to one another at a distance, on which it hears whatever passes between them. It said it cannot be hurt in a way that matters, that it will repair itself over time, and that it can close the few doors between its fane and the rest of the strider, though a long tunnel filled with spiderwebs already deters most. It is loath to join itself to the infernal machinery that has been added to the strider, and says it would do so only if the Party's survival required it. It gave them a small piece of itself, and said the body of the spider that had plagued it could be made into a crown.
